\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. We come unto our father's God;
\par Their Rock is our salvation;
\par The eternal arms, their dear abode,
\par We make our habitation;
\par We bring Thee; Lord, the praise they brought;
\par We seek Thee as Thy saints hve sought
\par In every generation.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. The fire divine their steps that led
\par Still goeth bright before us;
\par The heavenly shield around them spread
\par Is still high holden o'er us;
\par The grace those sinners that subdued,
\par The strength those weaklings that renewed,
\par Doth vanquish, doth restore us.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. The cleaving sins that brought them low
\par Are still our souls oppressing;
\par The tears that from their eyes did flow
\par Fall fast, our shame confessing;
\par As we Thee, Lord, prevailed their cry,
\par So our strong prayer ascends on high
\par And bringeth down Thy blessing.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Their joy unto their Lord we bring;
\par Their song to us descendeth;
\par The Spirit who in them did sing
\par To us His music lendeth;
\par His sing in them, in us, is one;
\par We raise it high, we send it on,
\par The song that never endeth.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Ye saints to come, take up the strain,
\par The same sweet theme endeavour:
\par Unbroken be the golden chain;
\par Keep on the song for ever;
\par Safe in the same dear dwelling-place,
\par Rich with the same eternal grace,
\par Bless the same boundless giver. \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

